Title: Fullscreen changes open the window again, and the OpenGL context follows every reopened window
Repository: SDL 3.4.12 with contrib SDL3-3.4.12-aros.diff (contrib 142b3ff4)
Date: 2026-11-21
Author: aros-sdl project
Problem: AROS_SetWindowFullscreen decided from SDL_WINDOW_FULLSCREEN in window->flags whether to open the Intuition window again, but SDL sets that flag only after the backend call. Entering fullscreen therefore left the window as it was until a later property change, and the window ran one step behind the requests. A size request for a fullscreen window resized it. A fullscreen mode with its own display mode closes all windows and the screen and opens them on a new screen; the OpenGL context stayed attached to the closed window and the next buffer swap drew into freed memory (alert "Semaphore in an illegal state", then a failure in gallium.library). Leaving such a mode failed to find a screen for the window (the restored desktop mode names a monitor, and the backend then tried to open a screen of its own for a window that is not fullscreen) and crashed in AROS_ShowWindow_Internal.
Change: AROS_SetWindowFullscreen compares the request with the state the backend holds and opens that window again when it differs; other open windows stay. AROS_ShowWindow_Internal attaches the current context to every window it opens (the call from patch 0015 moves there), reports the size a fullscreen window got, and returns when no screen is available. Size and position requests are not applied to a fullscreen window. On AROS a window that is not fullscreen always goes to the default public screen.
Scope: AROS (src/video/aros)
Upstream: candidate (contrib SDL3 port)
Verification: mainline x86_64 (nightly 2026-11-15), 2026-11-21, LOVE 12.0 with a program that calls love.window.updateMode in the order borderless, window, borderless, window, exclusive fullscreen, window, borderless, window. Before, on softpipe (pool slot v1-3): the borderless requests after the first changed nothing, exclusive fullscreen ended in the alert and the gallium.library failure; with the first part of the change, leaving exclusive fullscreen crashed in AROS_ShowWindow_Internal. After: all steps run to the end, the window is 800x600 in both fullscreen forms and 640x480 as a window each time, and every state draws. With VirtIO-GPU and VirGL (pool slot v1-4): window, borderless, window draw at the same sizes. The first frame after a change can be drawn for the previous size. Built for ABIv11 and Raspberry Pi, not run there.
Removal: when the contrib port carries the change
